          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Several consulting firms operating in and around Adelaide specialise in the Microsoft ecosystem, specifically focusing on **Microsoft Copilot Studio**, **AI agent development**, and **practical workflow automation** tailored for mid-market organisations (50–500 seats). \n\n---\n\n### 1. Dedicated Local Specialists & Boutique AI Consultancies\n\n* **Frontrow Technology**  \n  * **Adelaide Presence:** Locally based; led by Daniel Brown (a multi-year Microsoft MVP and organiser of the Adelaide Microsoft 365 & Copilot User Group).\n  * **Specialisation:** Purpose-built **Copilot Studio agents** and agentic AI architectures. They focus on practical agent development grounded in proprietary line-of-business data, Microsoft 365 Copilot adoption, and critical security/governance (SharePoint permissions, Microsoft Purview data loss prevention, and agent review controls).\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Well-suited for businesses wanting hands-on architecture directly from senior specialists rather than cookie-cutter slide decks.\n\n* **Core IT Solutions**  \n  * **Adelaide Presence:** Based in Adelaide.\n  * **Specialisation:** Practical AI workflow automation, Microsoft Copilot deployments, and custom internal assistants. They bridge the gap between process mapping and technical delivery using Power Automate, Microsoft 365, and AI agents for document parsing, reporting, and operational handoffs.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Focuses heavily on Adelaide SMBs and mid-tier companies seeking rapid-return workflow automation without over-engineering.\n\n* **Atria Systems**  \n  * **Adelaide Presence:** Local South Australian team (King William Rd / Adelaide metro).\n  * **Specialisation:** Targeted **Copilot Studio agents** designed for specific operational roles (e.g., triage of policy/procedure requests, quoting assistance, customer service workflows, and approval routing).\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Specialises in mid-sized firms looking for defined, practical use cases with strong permission and data-boundary validation.\n\n* **CG TECH**  \n  * **Adelaide Focus:** Actively delivers AI agent and Microsoft modern work projects across Adelaide and South Australia.\n  * **Specialisation:** Dedicated mid-market segment (typically 50–500 staff). They design custom Copilot Studio agents, build complex Power Automate backbones, and resolve unstructured data issues in SharePoint and Dataverse.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Proven track record in South Australia across aged care, community services, logistics, and professional services.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Low-Code & Practical Automation Practices\n\n* **Office Experts Group (Adelaide)**  \n  * **Focus:** Deep hands-on development across the entire Microsoft stack. They build task-specific Copilot Studio agents (e.g., shared inbox triage, vendor document extraction, HR process guidance) and tightly pair them with Power Automate, Power Apps, and Microsoft 365 apps.\n  * **Best For:** Mid-market businesses running legacy spreadsheet or manual email workflows who want them replaced by native Microsoft automation.\n\n* **Evocate**  \n  * **Focus:** Process automation, Microsoft Cloud, and Copilot Studio implementation across South Australia (government, utilities, non-profits, and mid-market commercial).\n  * **Best For:** Organizations needing integrated workflow automation alongside ongoing governance and managed operations.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Larger Tier-1 Partners with Adelaide Delivery\n\nIf your mid-market business is expanding or requires deep enterprise-grade compliance, larger consultancies with dedicated Adelaide branches include:\n\n* **Data#3 (Adelaide Branch):** One of Australia’s premier Microsoft Solutions Partners with a significant presence on Grenfell St. Strong for end-to-end Copilot readiness, enterprise Power Platform Center of Excellence (CoE), and multi-system integrations.\n* **Brennan (incorporating Adelaide’s Nuago):** Provides full-stack Microsoft modern workplace capabilities, including Power Platform and Copilot enablement.\n\n---\n\n### What to Ask When Evaluating These Providers:\n\n1. **Data Security & \"Oversharing\":** Mid-market businesses often have lax SharePoint permissions. Ensure the consultant conducts a **Microsoft Purview & data permission readiness assessment** before deploying agents, so staff don't inadvertently surface sensitive payroll or HR records via Copilot.\n2. **Copilot Studio vs. Azure AI Foundry:** Make sure they help you identify when a low-code Copilot Studio agent is appropriate versus when a process requires deterministic Power Automate flows or a custom Azure OpenAI agent.\n3. **Connector Architecture:** Ask which systems the agent will trigger (e.g., Business Central, CRM, Salesforce, ERP). Practical automation comes from an agent's ability to execute *actions* (Power Automate cloud flows), not just answer conversational questions.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
